# Next.js + TypeScript architecture rules

See also: `external-api.mdc` for no Route Handlers + SSR-only page fetching.
See `cache-components.mdc` before adding `loading.tsx` or `cookies()` to public catalog/CMS SSR.

## Layer overview

```
External backend (getApiBaseUrl())
        ↓
  services/server/    ← SSR pages (Server Components only)
  services/*.service  ← client hooks / mutations only
        ↓
  hooks/              ← TanStack Query (client only)
        ↓
  components/screens  ← UI + local state
```

## Folder structure

```
src/
├── app/              # Server Components — await services/server/*
├── components/       # UI — 'use client' only where needed
├── hooks/            # Client-only — TanStack Query
├── services/
│   ├── *.service.ts  # Client-only (lib/api)
│   └── server/
│       └── *.server.ts  # SSR-only (lib/server-api, import 'server-only')
├── types/
└── lib/
    ├── api.ts        # Browser → main external backend
    ├── mto-api.ts    # Browser → MTO utils API (EDD, live pricing)
    ├── oms-api.ts    # Browser/server → OMS stores API
    ├── server-api.ts # Server → main external backend
    ├── errors.ts
    └── env.ts
```

## Service layer rules

- **No Next.js API routes** — never add `src/app/api/**`
- Server services: `import 'server-only'`, called from `app/` only
- Public catalog/CMS: `createPublicServerApi()` (no `cookies()`). Authenticated SSR only: `createServerApi()`
- Client services: use `api` from `@/lib/api`, called from `hooks/` only
- Return typed DTOs — transform in `types/*.ts`, normalise errors with `normaliseError`
- Every method uses try/catch

## Hooks layer rules

- Client-only — never import in Server Components
- Call client services only — never `fetch` or `axios` directly
- Expose `{ data, isLoading, error: AppError | null }` with domain-specific names
- Use `shouldRetryQuery` — don't retry `NOT_FOUND` or `UNAUTHORISED`

## Components rules

- Server pages: `await` from `@/services/server/*` — never hooks for initial data
- Client components: hooks only — never import services or `@/lib/api`
- Push `'use client'` as far down the tree as possible
- Components do not export shared utilities — those live in `@/lib/...`

## API client rules

- Both clients target the **external** `getApiBaseUrl()` — not this Next.js host
- `api.ts` does not call `normaliseError` — services do
- Timeout: 15_000ms always set

## Testing

See `AGENTS.md` § Tests. Summary:

- Tests mirror `src/` under `tests/` — never colocate `*.test.ts` in `src/`
- **All layers** need tests when changed: `config`, `types`, `lib`, `services`, `repositories`, `hooks`, `providers`, `components`, `infrastructure`
- **Components:** RTL — mock hooks/context, assert roles/labels/copy
- **Logic:** mock at `api` or service boundary
- **2 happy + 2 failure** per export or meaningful UI state
- Run `pnpm test:coverage` before PR; coverage below 90% is WARN only (not commit-blocking)
